              = succeed "." do
                %strong strict monoidal functor
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              In the literature often the term “monoidal functor” refers by default to what in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LaxMonoidalFunctor"}
              is called a strong monoidal functor. With that convention then what def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LaxMonoidalFunctor"}
              calls a lax monoidal functor is called a
              = succeed "." do
                %strong weak monoidal functor
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              Lax monoidal functors are the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+morphisms"} lax morphisms
              for an appropriate
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-monad"} 2-monad
          .num_remark
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              An
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/oplax+monoidal+functor"} oplax monoidal functor
              (with various alternative names including
              = succeed ")," do
                %strong comonoidal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+categories"} opposite categories
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{op}
              to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi D
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^{op}
          .num_remark
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              A
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+transformation"} monoidal transformation
              between monoidal functors is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
              that respects the extra structure in an obvious way.
          %h2#properties Properties
          #MonoidsToMonoidsByLaxMonoidal.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (Lax monoidal functors send
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
