          %h3#relation_to_multicategories Relation to multicategories
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              Lax monoidal functors between monoidal categories are in correspondence with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism+of+multicategories"} morphisms
              between their underlying (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+multicategories"}> representable
              )
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multicategories"} multicategories
          %h3#relation_to_pros Relation to PROs
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_4 Remark
            %p
              Strong monoidal functors between monoidal categories are in correspondence with morphisms between their underlying (representable) colored
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/PROs"} PROs
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_5 Remark
            %p
              Strict monoidal functors between monoidal categories are in correspondence with morphisms between their underlying colored
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/PROs"} PROs
              that preserve the distinguished isomorphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ∼
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} () \xrightarrow{\sim} I
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
