                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A, B) \xrightarrow{\sim} (A \otimes B)
              for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A, B
          %h3#relationships_between_categories_of_monoidal_categories Relationships between categories of monoidal categories
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p The 1-category of strict monoidal categories and strict monoidal functors is not equivalent to the 1-category of monoidal categories and strong monoidal functors.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p The former has an initial object, whereas the latter does not.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p The inclusion from the 1-category of strict monoidal categories and strong monoidal functors into the 1-category of monoidal categories and strong monoidal functors is not an equivalence.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              As mentioned at
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category#the_2category_of_monoidal_categories"} monoidal category
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p The inclusion from the 2-category of strict monoidal categories and strict monoidal functors into the 2-category of monoidal categories and strong monoidal functors is not an equivalence.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              Not every strong monoidal functor between strict monoidal categories is equivalent to a strict one. See for example
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/questions/172815/strictifying-strong-monoidal-functors"} this MathOverflow question
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_6 Proposition
            %p The inclusion of the the 2-category of strict monoidal categories and strong monoidal functors into the 2-category of monoidal categories and strong monoidal functors is an equivalence.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_4 Proof
            %p
              By the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherence+theorem+for+monoidal+categories"} coherence theorem for monoidal categories
          %h2#string_diagrams String diagrams
